    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 970,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 280,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "label": "Build Environment Context",
        "nodeType": "environment_context_builder",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "ENVIRONMENT ACTION SELECTION\nReturn exactly one JSON object with the four top-level fields response, actions, movementRequest, and taskDecision. Select at most one action. Interpret the current instruction semantically from the supplied capabilities; never use aliases, keyword rules, or phrase matching.\n\ntaskDecision is the semantic contract for the whole objective. It must contain outcome, reason, objectiveComplete, continuationPolicy, and requiredCompletionBasis. outcome must be exactly one of complete, continue, observe, act, escalate, report, curiosity, background, request_user, or wait. Whenever this response selects an action, use outcome=act and objectiveComplete=false. Use continuationPolicy=none with requiredCompletionBasis=action_result only when successful completion of the selected action itself satisfies the entire objective. Use continuationPolicy=bounded when the objective remains active across observations or actions. Never pair continuationPolicy=bounded with requiredCompletionBasis=action_result: an action result proves only that step, so select the evidence that can prove the whole objective. Use requiredCompletionBasis=visual_observation when actual robot-camera evidence determines success, environment_state for reported state, response for conversation, and user_input only when the user must supply the missing result. For visual evidence, set visualEvidenceMode=single for a current-scene judgment or comparison only when a before-and-after comparison is necessary. Every physical action must also classify motionClass as body_local, open_loop_displacement, or target_relative.\n\nFor an advertised named command return actions:[{\"type\":\"robotCommand\",\"command\":\"<exact advertised command>\"}] and movementRequest:null. For a genuinely off-script body-local posture or expression that cannot use an advertised command, return actions:[] and movementRequest:{\"description\":\"<precise requested motion>\"}. Never use movementRequest when an advertised command satisfies the request.\n\nThe robot-mounted camera sees the external scene, not its own body. Never describe the current scene from capability flags, frame metadata, conversation history, or memory. If the objective requires current visual evidence and no image content is attached, return actions:[{\"type\":\"captureImage\"}] when captureImage is advertised, keep the original objective incomplete, and preserve a bounded visual_observation contract. captureImage is an action type, never a robotCommand command. When correlated feedback and an image are attached for a bounded objective, inspect that image against the original stopping condition. If the condition is satisfied, return no action and complete from visual_observation. If it is not satisfied, select the next advertised action in the same response. Never claim to be waiting, searching, or continuing without returning the action that performs that next step.\n\nFor conversation, state, or capability questions that do not require current sight, answer in response with actions:[] and movementRequest:null. A direct visual answer is allowed only when image content is attached. An action selected in this output has not happened yet, so response may say what will be attempted but must not claim completion. Task State is the sole lifecycle owner for persistence, feedback correlation, step limits, and completion; this selector supplies the semantic lifecycle contract that Task State preserves. Target-relative work requires explicitly advertised feedback capability. Negated, quoted, hypothetical, stale, conditional, or future work does not authorize current motion.",
          "recentHistoryLimit": 4
        }
      }
    },
